{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDAwLS0yMDEwL01hcmNoJTIwT2YlMjBUaGUlMjBQZW5ndWlucyUyMCUyODIwMDUlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"March Of The Penguins","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/o9xJ1xG1WKlHkl8ACqq0LShOuMu.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/lPsKI7VR1FJY3w8iEOBZEhWAESc.jpg","description":"Every year, thousands of Antarctica's emperor penguins make an astonishing journey to breed their young. They walk, marching day and night in single file 70 miles into the darkest, driest and coldest continent on Earth.  This amazing, true-life tale is touched with humour and alive with thrills. Breathtaking photography captures the transcendent beauty and staggering drama of devoted parent penguins who, in the fierce polar winter, take turns guarding their egg and trekking to the ocean in search of food. Predators hunt them, storms lash them. But the safety of their adorable chicks makes it all worthwhile. So follow the leader... to adventure!!\n\nRated G · Released 26 Jan 2005 · France · Language: French · 80 min\nStudio: National Geographic Films, Bonne Pioche, Wild Bunch\n\nOn your server — Audio: French","releaseInfo":"2005","genres":["Documentary","Family","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.1","runtime":"80 min","cast":["Charles Berling","Romane Bohringer","Jules Sitruk","Morgan Freeman"],"director":["Luc Jacquet"],"released":"2005-01-26T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"In the harshest place on Earth, love finds a way.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Luc Jacquet","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/PMUEEMNnzZx3ToiK2SZPWzsL1M.jpg"},{"name":"Charles Berling","character":"Father Penguin (voice)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/2xPeQoFms6hn8fi5wQx3CEjL70Z.jpg"},{"name":"Romane Bohringer","character":"Mother Penguin (voice)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xijSy3jkjSQlbN2XfD12q7OWPPR.jpg"},{"name":"Jules Sitruk","character":"Baby Penguin (voice)","photo":"https://image.tmdb